# cw178, the hooded counter-keeper (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle cw178
revision 1
state ready
dialect coldwater
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rm_lotte_ashford
written_by claude
title the hooded counter-keeper
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=merchant honesty=guarded
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=guarded piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk never_goes_out_without_an_oilcloth_hood
likes crisp_apples dancing festival_bells summer_evenings
dislikes bad_manners salt_wind
fears saying_the_wrong_thing_to_the_wrong_ears
hopes a_feast_day_with_no_rain
topics festival +0.4 weather +0.3 pastimes +0.3 work +0.2 gossip -0.5 crime -0.3
styles comfort=practical gossip=closed refuse=firm tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# keeps the counter of a family workshop in the Commons: guarded and plain-spoken, loud about manners and silent about everything else, never out of doors without an oilcloth hood, and the first on the green when the feast-day bells ring.

words
oath! = Oilcloth and oak | Hood and hinge
saying! = A shut mouth catches no rain | Manners first, then talk
hood = my oilcloth hood | the hood
sky = the sky | this lying sky
apple = an apple fresh off the cart | a hard red apple
bells = the feast-day bells | bells ringing for a feast
reel = a reel | a turn on the green
dusk = a summer dusk | a long warm dusk
manners = manners | a civil tongue
saltwind = the wind off the sea | that salty wind
counter = the counter | our counter
shavings = the shavings | curls of shavings
lake = the lake | Glasswater
mist = the mist | the lake-mist
counsel = my own counsel | my thoughts to myself
pup = the pup | my little one

any
opinion @1 newcomers for 1 : New faces mean new custom at #counter#. I'm not too grand to take their coin, if they ask for things nicely.
opinion @1 city against 1 : Ten years on one street and I couldn't tell you who's behind half the doors. That's the city's idea of #manners#.
opinion @1 watch mixed 0 : #watch.capitalize# sees what it's paid to see. That's the end of what I'll say, and I'll say it quiet.
opinion @1 festivals for 2 : A feast day is the one day this city has #manners#. Everybody says good morning when #bells# are ringing.
opinion @1 houses mixed 0 : I've thoughts about the Houses. They stay in my head, under #hood#.
opinion @1 strangers mixed 1 : I'll be civil to any stranger who's civil first. #saying.capitalize#.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. Wipe your feet, please. | #greet#, #address#. Mind the step down.
line @2 greet [self.working=yes self.job=merchant] : #greet#. Name the piece, and I'll fetch the rule. | #greet#. Wait a moment; I'll be with you.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. #mist.capitalize# on the roofs still. | Morning, #address#. Early, and civil with it.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. Hood up; there'll be #rain# before you're home. | #greet#. Late to be out, #address#.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : There you are. Shoes off; I've swept #shavings# out. | Come in. Kettle's hot.
line @1 again.open : You again. I'll put the kettle back on, #address#. | Back so soon. You must like #counter#.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. | #greet#, #address#.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : #greet#. Shake off; you're dripping. | #greet#. Good; it's you and not a customer.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes] : #greet#. One moment; I'm with a customer. | #greet#. Mind the shavings.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. | #farewell#. Hood up, now.
line @2 farewell [here.time=dusk|night] : #farewell#. Lamplit streets only, mind. | #farewell#. Calm water to you, and a dry walk home.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#. | #farewell#, #address#. Mind the step.
line @1 react.news : #surprise#. Is it certain? | That's news. It goes no further than me.
line @1 react.news.new : #surprise#. I'd not heard. | That's new to me. It stays under #hood#.
line @1 react.news.known : #knew#. Ears open, mouth shut; that's me. | I'd heard. I kept #counsel#.
line @1 react.news.doubt : #doubt#. I'll wait till it's proven. | #hedge#. Talk's cheap; I'll wait for the facts.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : #pity#. I'm sorry for it. | That's #bad#. Poor souls.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : #gladnews#. There'll be a feast, then. | #good.capitalize#. I'm glad, and I'll say so.
line @1 answer.how : Well enough. Dry under #hood#, at least. | #fine#. Busy, and keeping it that way.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : #busy.capitalize#. The orders don't stop. | #tired.capitalize#, and it's not noon.
line @1 ask.how : And you, #address#? Not soaked yet, I hope. | How are you keeping, #address#?
line @1 sympathise : #sympathy#. Sit down a minute. | I'm sorry. I'll not pry. Tell me only what you want to.
line @1 reassure : #reassure#. It'll blow over. | It'll come right. Even #sky# clears, now and then.
line @1 decline [self.working=yes] : #hedge#, but no. I can't leave #counter# untended, and there's nobody else today. | I'd like to, but the orders at #counter# won't write themselves up.
line @2 decline : Not this time, #address#. I've my own door to get home to. | No, thank you kindly. I keep to home of an evening, and that's that.
line @1 accept_decline : #no_matter#. Another time. | That's all right. It'll keep.
line @1 thank : #thanks#. That was civil of you. | #manners.capitalize# like that, I remember.
line @1 deflect_thanks : #deflect#. | It was only #manners#.
line @1 preclose [self.working=yes] : Well. #counter.capitalize# won't mind itself. | Back to #counter#; there's a customer.
line @2 preclose : Well. #preclose#. | I'll be off before #rain# comes. It always comes.
line @1 accept_preclose : Go on, then. Hood up. | #bc_fair_enough# Mind the wet.
line @1 ack : #bc_true# | Mm. #bc_right#
line @1 give.advice : #advise#: never leave home without a hood in this city. The sky lies. | Say please and thank you. #manners.capitalize# will open more doors than coin.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : #warn#. Keep inside the walls. | Don't go past the gates, #address#. Not this week.
scene hood_on_clear_day
when topic=weather|smalltalk here.weather=clear here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : Clear as glass, and I've #hood# on. You'll see why by noon. | Folk laugh at me for wearing #hood# in the sun. They stop laughing at the first drop. | Not a cloud. I don't trust it. #sky.capitalize# has fooled me before.
b : It looks fine to me. | Do they? | Has it?
a : It always does, till it doesn't. #sky.capitalize# rains out of nothing here. | Every time. Then they ask where I bought it. | My first week here. Sun at dawn, soaked by noon. Never again.
b : #bc_ha# | #bc_fair_enough# | #bc_wise#

scene hood_vindicated
when topic=weather here.weather=rain here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : There. Rain. And who's dry? #oath#. | Look at them running. Not one hood among them. | #rain.capitalize# again. I'd say I told them, but nobody listens.
b : You were right. | It's coming down hard. | I should've listened.
a : I usually am, about #sky#. Not much else. | Hard and cold. #hood.capitalize# keeps the worst off. | You should. Oilcloth's cheap. A chill isn't.

scene salt_wind_hood
when topic=weather here.region=ridgemere self.dislikes=salt_wind
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess / ack
a : #saltwind.capitalize# again. It gets under #hood# and into everything. | #saltwind.capitalize# leaves salt on my whiskers. I wash and it's back. | At #home# the wind smelled of fresh water. Here it smells of brine and fish.
b : It's the sea. | Annoying stuff. | I like the smell.
a : It is. I'd swap it for #lake# tomorrow. | Annoying, and it rots the wood. Ask any joiner. | You're welcome to it. I'll keep my hood up.
b? : #bc_true# | #bc_mine_too# | #bc_ha#

scene counter_customers
when topic=work self.working=yes self.job=merchant
does tell.self / react.self / assess / ack
a : I keep #counter# at #self.workplace#. Orders in, coin in, and the shavings swept. | Somebody wanted a chair for Restday. I told them a fortnight. They'll get it in a fortnight. | I write every order down at #counter#. If it's not on paper, it wasn't asked for.
b[job=merchant] #trade : Paper saves arguments. | They always want it sooner. | Every order? Sensible.
b : Busy work. | Did they take it? | That's careful.
a@trade : It does. And it saves my temper. | Always. Never once has sooner been possible. | Sensible saves trouble. #saying.capitalize#.
a : Busy, and better busy than idle. | They took it. They didn't like it. | Careful keeps a shop. Careless closes one.
b? : #bc_true# | #bc_ha# | #bc_wise#

scene no_please
when topic=smalltalk|work self.dislikes=bad_manners
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / insist / ack
a : A fellow came up to me in the street and pointed at #hood#. Not a word. Just pointed. | Somebody pushed in front of an old wolf at the stall. I said something. Loudly. | No please, no thank you, and he wanted it cheap. #oath#.
b : Rude. | Good for you. | Did you sell it?
a : Rude, and I told him so. He found his words quick enough. | Somebody had to. #manners.capitalize# won't cost you a farthing. | At full price. #saying.capitalize#.
b : #bc_ha# | #bc_good# | #bc_ha#

scene what_i_see
when topic=crime|lore here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : I see a lot from my doorstep. Who the Watch walks past, and who they don't. | Some doors in this city never get knocked on. I notice which. | I keep #counsel# about this town. It's safer.
b : Who do they walk past? | Which doors? | Safer how?
a : I'll not say. I've a door I'd like to keep. It stays under #hood#. | Big ones. That's all you'll get from me. | Some folk don't like being noticed. I'd rather not be noticed noticing.
b : #bc_fair_enough# | #bc_wise# | #bc_true#

scene closed_mouth
when topic=gossip
does tell.gossip / react.news / insist / ack
a : Plenty's said in my hearing. None of it leaves with me. | Don't ask me what folk say. I've ears, not a mouth for it. | Gossip's like rain. It gets on everybody. I keep #hood# up.
b : Not even a little? | Go on. | Ha. Fair.
a : Not a word. #saying.capitalize#. | No. Find somebody looser. | Fair, and dry. #hood.capitalize# stays up.
b? : #bc_ha# | #bc_fair_enough# | #bc_ha#

scene spouse_kept
when topic=family self.married=yes self.spouse
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #self.spouse# and I go whole evenings without a word. We don't need any. | I'd not swap #self.spouse# for a House and its lands. Don't tell #self.spouse#. | My #self.spouse_word# would tell you I'm hard to know. My #self.spouse_word# would be right.
b : That's a good marriage. | I'll not tell. | And easy to love?
a : Good enough to last. | Thank you. It'd go to the head. | That's not for me to say. #oath#.

scene the_pup
when topic=family self.parent=yes self.child
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #self.child# is cleverer than me already. I'll not say that where #self.child# can hear. | I worry about #self.child# out in this city. I make #self.child# wear a hood. | I want #self.child# to have #manners# before anything. The rest can come after.
b : Clever pups are trouble. | And is it worn? | Good manners last.
a : They are. I was one. | When I'm watching. #oath#. | They do. Longer than coin.

scene hard_apples
when topic=food self.likes=crisp_apples
does offer / accept / assess / ack
a : Here, take #apple#. I bought too many again. | Nothing like #apple# with a snap to it. Soft ones I give to the cart horse. | I've a bag of apples by the door. Help yourself.
b : Thank you. | Lucky horse. | I will.
a : Mind the core; it's a hard one. | Luckier than most. | Take two. I'll only buy more.
b? : #bc_good# | #bc_ha# | #bc_thank_you#

scene feast_bells
when topic=festival|day self.likes=festival_bells
does tell.feeling / ask.opinion / give.opinion / assess
a : When #bells# go, I put my hood down. That's the only day I do. | #bells.capitalize#. Best noise in the city. Even I'll smile at a stranger. | I'm up before #bells# on a feast day, waiting.
b : The only day? | Even you? | Waiting for what?
a : The only day. #sky.capitalize# behaves on a feast. Mostly. | Even me. Don't spread it. | For the first peal. Then the whole street comes out.
b : #bc_lovely# | #bc_ha# | Sounds a fine morning.

scene reel_on_green
when topic=pastimes|festival self.likes=dancing
does tell.self / react.self / assess / ack
a : Folk think I'm stiff. Put me in #reel# and see. | I'll dance with anybody who asks nicely. #manners.capitalize# first, then feet. | The one place I don't keep #counsel# is on the green, dancing.
b : You dance? | Anybody? | What do you tell?
a : Every reel at the feast. I don't sit down. | Anybody civil. I turned down a toff who didn't bow. | Nothing. My feet tell it. That's different.
b? : #bc_ha# | #bc_good# | #bc_ha#

scene summer_dusk
when topic=season|day here.season=summer here.time=dusk self.likes=summer_evenings
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #dusk.capitalize#, and for once I've #hood# down. | The street's shut up and the light won't go. This is the hour I'd keep. | Sit out with me. A summer evening's too good to waste indoors.
b : It's warm still. | It's a good hour. | I will.
a : Warm and dry. Here, that's rare as a toff's thank-you. | It is. The street's quiet and nobody's rude. | Good. Mind the step; it's still warm from the sun.

scene lake_away
when topic=memories|travel self.away=yes self.from=coldwater
does tell.memory / react.self / assess
a : At home the rain came off #lake# slow and soft. Here it comes sideways off the sea. | I miss #mist# on the water at dawn. Still water, flat as a table. | I left #self.from_town# by my own choice. Don't let anybody tell you otherwise.
b[from=coldwater] #home : Lake rain. I know it. | The still water. This sea never stops moving. | Nobody would.
b : Do you miss it? | Sounds peaceful. | Did you choose well?
a@home : That's why I keep a hood on, here. | We'll not see it again, likely. #oath#. | Good. I'd not stand for it.
a : The #rain#, oddly. Only that. | It was. Too peaceful, some days. | Well enough. I'd do it again.

scene talk_kept
when topic=accent self.away=yes self.from=coldwater
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Calm water, I tell customers. Half the Commons think I'm wishing them luck at sea. | My lake words come out when I'm cross. Customers learn quick. | I keep my old talk for home. Out of doors I'm plain as a plank.
b : Aren't you? | What words? | Plain as a plank?
a : Near enough. It's a kind thing to wish anyone. | Weed and tangle, mostly. They take the hint. | It's a joiners' saying. I've caught it off them, living here.

scene chapel_quiet
when topic=faith
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : Restday chapel, and my prayers kept to myself. The Bright One knows them already. | Each dry walk home, I say thank you to the Bright One under my breath. Not often needed, some weeks. | I pray quiet. Some folk pray like they want the street to hear.
b : That's enough. | Not often? | Some do.
a : I hope so. I'll not shout them. | This city rains six days in seven. I thank where I can. #oath#. | They do. There's #manners# wanted in chapel too.

scene new_custom
when topic=newcomer self.job=merchant
does tell.self / react.self / assess / ack
a : #topic.subject.capitalize#'s just moved onto the street, they say. New faces need chairs. | Every week there's new faces in the Commons, and near half find #counter# for a stool. | I like newcomers who say good morning. I'll give them a fair price.
b : Good for trade. | Half? | And the others?
a : It is. I'll be civil, and see if they are. | Near half. A stool's the first thing anyone buys. | Full price. #saying.capitalize#.
b : #bc_good# | #bc_ha# | #bc_ha#

scene thin_month
when topic=times|prices world.times=hard|lean self.job=merchant
does tell.worry / reassure / assess / ack
a : Thin month at #counter#. Folk are mending chairs instead of buying new. | Orders are down. #counter.capitalize# is quiet as a chapel. | Everyone's tight. I don't blame them. I'm tight too.
b : It'll turn. | Quiet's not always bad. | It'll ease.
a : It will. Chairs break. They always break. #reassure#. | It is when the rent's due. | It will. I'll keep #counsel# till then.
b? : #bc_i_hope_so# | #bc_true# | #bc_i_hope_so#

story first_week_rain [topic=memories|weather self.away=yes here.region=ridgemere]
  : My first morning in this city it was sun from end to end. I left my hood behind.
  : By noon I was wet to the skin. I walked into the first shop I saw and bought oilcloth.
  ask : Have you ever been caught that badly?
  b : Every week, nearly. I never learn.
  b[old] : Once. Then I bought a hood like yours.
  : I've not been out without it since. #saying.capitalize#, and a hood's the other half of it.

story bells_morning [topic=festival|memories self.married=yes self.age>=25]
  : The morning I was wed, #bells# were ringing for a feast. Nothing to do with us.
  : I told everybody they were ringing for me, and nobody argued.
  ask : Would you have argued?
  b : Not on your wedding day.
  : Nobody did. #oath#. I still take them as mine, every feast.

story pushed_in [topic=smalltalk|memories self.dislikes=bad_manners]
  : A toff pushed in front of me at the bakers once, cloak and all.
  : I said, with the whole queue listening, that there was a line, and the end of it was behind me.
  ask : Would you have said it?
  b : I'd have thought it.
  : The toff went red as a beet and went to the back. Good manners cost nothing. Forgetting them costs a face.

rule @hood_bark
when concept=bark here.region=ridgemere
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Hood up. #rain.capitalize# by noon. | #sky.capitalize#. I don't trust it.

rule @manners_bark
when concept=bark self.dislikes=bad_manners
does aside
cooldown 10h
say A please wouldn't kill you, #fool#. | #oath#. Manners, somebody.

rule @salt_bark
when concept=bark self.dislikes=salt_wind
does aside
cooldown 10h
say #saltwind.capitalize#. Salt on my whiskers again. | Wind's off the sea. Hood up.

rule @shop_bark
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=merchant
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Orders taken at #counter#. Chairs, stools, shelves. | Mind the shavings by the door.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. What is it you need? | #greet#, #address#. Wipe your feet.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #greet#, #topic.player#. Civil of you to come back.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : It's late, #address#. I'll hear you, briefly.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : State your business. Civilly, if you please.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.working=yes self.job=merchant] : I keep the counter at #self.workplace#. Orders, accounts, and the sweeping.
dlg @2 resident.job : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. That's all I'll say about it. | #job_busy#
dlg @1 resident.news [!world.news !world.event_words world.wagons!=raided world.death!=recent world.wedding!=recent] : #news_none# And if there were, I'd keep it. | Nothing I'd repeat.
dlg @2 resident.news [world.news] : Word from #world.news_from#: #world.news#. No more than that.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : They say #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. You'll not hear it from me again.
dlg @2 resident.gossip [here.gossip!=yes] : #gossip_none# | I keep #counsel#. Ask someone else.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. Hood up, now. | #farewell#, #address#.
graft resident.hub
choice Why the hood, on a day like this? [here.region=ridgemere] -> hood
node hood
say Because this city lies. Sun at dawn, soaked by noon. I learned that my first week, and I've not been out without oilcloth since.
mood calm
free
choice Does it ever stay dry? -> hood_dry
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node hood_dry
say On a feast day, sometimes. Then I put the hood down and dance. That's the only time you'll see my ears.
choice I'll look out for it. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
